## Geometry Lemma Target
Audited finite form:
  Each small-touch/no-hard row has an edgeless dead-cover projection.
  Every dead projection node is a rank-2 singleton pocket with one B0
  owner and one B1 owner, and every such pocket has an exact mirror
  partner.  Five rows have one mirror pair; random_covering_001 has two.
  No row has a hard mirror orbit.  The S319 split separates two
  delta-sidecar pockets (039,074) from four branch-unit singleton rows
  (001,062,086,101).
Proof pull:
  replace graph edge-current by a singleton-pocket theorem: a mirror pair
  of rank-2 isolated dead components with unique owner labels cannot be
  terminally bad once its complete/touching E-branch gate sidecar and
  owner-pair residue/span word are retained.  The four unit rows should
  be the first proof target; the two S319 delta-sidecar rows need the
  extra cover-delta sidecar.

